hadiths[97]{hadithnumber,text}:
"228","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to relate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(One night) the roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah, then Jibreel (peace be upon him) descended and split open my chest, then washed it with the water of Zamzam, then brought a golden basin filled with wisdom and faith and poured it into my chest, then closed it up. After that, he took my hand and ascended with me to the heavens. When I reached the lowest heaven, Jibreel (peace be upon him) said to the gatekeeper of the heaven, ‘Open (the gate).’ He asked, ‘Who is this?’ He replied, ‘This is Jibreel.’ He asked, ‘Is there anyone with you?’ Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ‘Yes! Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is with me.’ He asked, ‘Has he been called?’ Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ‘Yes.’ So when the gate was opened, we ascended to the lowest heaven. Suddenly, I saw a man sitting, with some people on his right and some on his left. When he looked to his right, he laughed, and when he looked to his left, he wept. Then he (upon seeing me) said, ‘Welcome, O righteous Prophet and righteous son!’ I asked Jibreel (peace be upon him), ‘Who is this?’ He said, ‘This is Adam (peace be upon him), and those on his right and left are the souls of his offspring. The people on his right are the people of Paradise, and those on his left are the people of Hell. That is why when he looks to his right, he laughs, and when he looks to his left, he weeps.’ Then I was taken up to the second heaven, and its gatekeeper was told to open the gate, and he spoke in the same manner as the previous one. Then the gate was opened. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that then Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) met Adam, Idris, Musa, Isa, and Ibrahim (peace be upon them) in the heavens (and did not mention their places except that he said) he found Adam (peace be upon him) in the lowest heaven and Ibrahim (peace be upon him) in the sixth heaven. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when Jibreel (peace be upon him) took the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) past Idris (peace be upon him), he said, ‘Welcome, O righteous Prophet and righteous brother.’ (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) I asked Jibreel (peace be upon him), ‘Who is this?’ He said, ‘This is Idris (peace be upon him).’ Then I passed by Musa (peace be upon him), and he said to me, ‘Welcome, O righteous Prophet and righteous brother.’ I asked (Jibreel), ‘Who is this?’ He said, ‘This is Musa (peace be upon him).’ Then I passed by Isa (peace be upon him), and he said, ‘Welcome, O righteous Prophet and righteous brother.’ I asked, ‘Who is this?’ He said, ‘This is Isa (peace be upon him).’ Then I passed by Ibrahim (peace be upon him), and he said, ‘Welcome, O righteous Prophet and righteous son.’ I asked, ‘Who is this?’ Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ‘This is Ibrahim (peace be upon him).’ (The narrator said) Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas and Abu Habba Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them) say that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then I was taken up further until I reached a very high place where I could hear the sound of the pens (writing of the angels). Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then Allah made fifty prayers obligatory upon my Ummah. So I returned with them until I passed by Musa (peace be upon him), and he asked, ‘What has Allah made obligatory upon your Ummah?’ I said, ‘Fifty prayers have been made obligatory.’ He said, ‘Return to your Lord, for your Ummah will not be able to bear that.’ So I returned, and Allah reduced a portion of it. Then I returned to Musa (peace be upon him) and said, ‘Allah has reduced a portion of it.’ Musa (peace be upon him) said, ‘Return to your Lord, for your Ummah will not be able to bear that.’ So I returned, and Allah reduced a portion of it (again). Then I returned to him (and informed him), and he said, ‘Return to your Lord, for your Ummah will not be able to bear that.’ So I returned again to Allah, and Allah said: ‘(Fine) These are five (prayers), and they are (in reward) as fifty, and My word does not change with Me.’ Then I returned to Musa (peace be upon him), and he said, ‘Return to your Lord.’ I said, ‘Now I feel shy before my Lord (to keep returning).’ (Then Jibreel took me and brought me to Sidrat al-Muntaha, and it was covered with many colors, I do not know what they were.) Then I was taken into Paradise, and (I saw that) its domes were pearls and its soil was musk.”"
"229","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When Allah made the prayer obligatory, it was prescribed as two rak'ahs, both in residence and on a journey. Then the prayer during travel was kept as it was, and an addition was made to the prayer in residence."
"230","Narrated from Sayyiduna Umar bin Abi Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered prayer in a single garment, having separated its two ends (i.e., he turned it and placed it over his shoulders)."
"231","Lady Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with her) says that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrapped himself in a single cloth and performed eight units (rak‘ahs) of (Duha) prayer."
"232","Lady Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) says in this narration that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah, wrapped himself in a single cloth and performed eight units of prayer. When he finished, I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My mother's son (Sayyidina Ali, may Allah be pleased with him) says that he will kill a man, even though I have granted him protection—the son of Hubayrah, so-and-so."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Umm Hani! Whom you have granted protection, we have also granted protection."" Umm Hani says that this (prayer) was the forenoon (Duha) prayer."
"233","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that a questioner asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about praying in a single garment, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does each one of you have two garments?"
"234","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should pray in a single garment with nothing on his shoulders."
"235","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays in a single garment should separate its two ends (i.e., place the right end on the left shoulder and the left end on the right shoulder)."
"236","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys. One night, due to a need of mine, I came to him and found him praying. I had a cloth over my body, so I wrapped it tightly around myself and stood by his side and prayed as well. When he finished, he said: ""O Jabir! What brings you at this hour of the night?"" I told him my need. When I was done, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What was that wrapping of the cloth that I saw?"" I said: It was a single cloth. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If the cloth is wide, then wrap yourself in it, and if it is tight, then make it an izar (lower garment or waist-wrapper)."
"237","Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some people used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), tying their lower garments over their shoulders like children, and the women were told not to raise their heads until the men sat up straight. (Because the men had only one garment, there was a fear of exposure.)"
"238","Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on a journey, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Mughirah! Pick up the water container.” So I picked it up. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) walked until he was out of my sight and relieved himself. At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was wearing a Syrian cloak. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) tried to take his hand out from its sleeve, it was tight, so he took his hand out from underneath it. Then I poured water over the noble limbs of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he performed ablution just as he would for prayer, and he wiped over his leather socks, then he prayed."
"239","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying stones along with the Quraysh for the (re)construction of the Ka'bah, and he (peace be upon him) had his waist-wrapper (tied) around his (blessed) body. His uncle, Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), said to him: ""O my nephew! If only you would remove your waist-wrapper and place it on your shoulders under the stone."" Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Prophet (peace be upon him) untied his waist-wrapper and placed it on his shoulders, and then he fell unconscious and collapsed. After that, he (peace be upon him) was never seen naked."
"240","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wrapping oneself tightly with a single garment and from sitting in a single garment in such a way that no part of it covers his private parts."
"241","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two (types of) sales: 'Lamas' (touching) and 'Nabadh' (throwing), and from wrapping oneself tightly (ishtimal-e-samma) and from sitting with only one garment wrapped around the body."
"242","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says:` Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) sent me during that Hajj (which was performed before the Farewell Pilgrimage and in which Sayyiduna Abu Bakr was the leader of all) with the announcers on the Day of Sacrifice so that we could proclaim in Mina that after this year no polytheist should perform Hajj and no one should circumambulate the Ka'bah naked. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) after Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) and ordered him to announce Surah Bara'ah. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that thus Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) announced among the people of Mina with us on the Day of Sacrifice: ""After this year, no polytheist should perform Hajj and no one should circumambulate (the Ka'bah) naked."
"243","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought in the battle of Khaybar, and we offered the morning prayer near Khaybar in the darkness. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted (his ride), and Sayyiduna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) also mounted, and I was riding behind Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded through the streets of Khaybar, and my knee kept touching the thigh of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he removed his lower garment from his thigh until I began to see the whiteness of the thigh of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he entered the valley and said: “Allah is the Greatest! Khaybar is ruined! Whenever we descend upon the courtyard of a people (for battle), then evil is the morning for those who have been warned.” He said this three times. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The people (of Khaybar) came out for their work and said, “Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come, and the army (has also come).” So we conquered Khaybar by force of the sword. Then the captives were gathered, and Sayyiduna Dihyah (may Allah be pleased with him) came and said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Give me a slave woman from among the captives.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Go and take any slave woman.” He took Safiyyah bint Huyayy. Then a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! You have given Safiyyah, the chief lady of the tribes of Qurayzah and Nadir, to Dihyah (may Allah be pleased with him), and she is suitable only for you.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Bring Safiyyah here.” When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Safiyyah, he said (to Dihyah): “Take another slave woman from among the captives instead of her.” (Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, says:) Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set Safiyyah free and married her. When they set out on the way, Umm Sulaym adorned Umm al-Mu’minin Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sent her to him at night. In the morning, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as a bridegroom, said: “Whoever has anything, let him bring it.” And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spread out a leather mat. Some brought dates, and some brought clarified butter. (The narrator says:) I think Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) also mentioned sattu (roasted barley flour). (Then) he says: Then they mixed all of it and made malidah (a dish of dates, butter, and flour), and that was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"244","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead the Fajr prayer, and several Muslim women, wrapped in their sheets, would attend with him. Then they would return to their homes at such a time that (due to the darkness) no one could recognize them."
"245","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed in a decorated cloak which had designs on it, and his gaze fell upon its designs. Then when he finished, he said: ""Take this cloak to Abu Juham and bring me Abu Juham's plain cloak, because this (decorated cloak) has distracted me from my prayer."
"246","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) had a curtain with which she had covered a corner of her house. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Remove this curtain from us, for its images keep appearing before me during prayer."
"247","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a silk cloak (a coat, a type of garment worn over clothes) was presented as a gift to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He wore it and performed prayer in it. Then, when he finished, he pulled it off forcefully, as if he disliked it, and said: ""It does not befit the pious."
"248","Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a red leather tent, and I saw Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) that he brought water for ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw the people that they began to take that ablution (water) hand to hand. Then whoever got some of it would rub it on his face, and whoever did not get any would take moisture from his companion’s hand. Then I saw Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) that he picked up a small spear and fixed it in the ground, and the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out wearing a red garment (lifting his cloak), and performed two rak‘ahs of prayer with the people towards the spear, and I saw the people and animals passing in front of the spear (here the spear or ‘anza was used as a sutrah)."
"249","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked, “What was the (Prophet’s) pulpit made of?” He replied, “There is no one among the people who knows this matter better than me (now). It was made of tamarisk wood from the forest of Ghaba. A slave woman’s servant made it for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When it was constructed and placed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood on it, faced the Qiblah, and said the opening Takbir. The people stood behind him. Then he recited (Qur’an), bowed (in Ruku’), and the people bowed behind him. Then he raised his blessed head, then stepped back until he prostrated on the ground. Then he ascended the pulpit again, recited (Qur’an), bowed, then raised his head and stepped back until he prostrated on the ground. Thus, this was the story of the pulpit.”"
"250","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that his grandmother, Malikah (may Allah be pleased with her), invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to eat, which she had specially prepared for him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from it, then said: ""Stand up, I will pray for you."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I turned to a mat of mine which had become black due to excessive use, so I washed it with water. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on it, and I and an orphan formed a row behind him, and the old woman was behind us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in two rak‘ahs and then returned."
"251","‘Aisha, the Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), says: I used to sleep in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and my feet would be in the place where he performed prostration. When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would prostrate, he would press me, and I would draw in my feet. When he stood up, I would stretch them out again. Umm al-Mu’minin ‘Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: At that time, there were no lamps in the houses."
"252","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray on his bedding at home, and she (i.e., Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) would be lying on the bedding between him (peace be upon him) and the place of prostration, in the manner of a bier."
"253","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and some of us would spread the edge of our garment on the place of prostration because of the intense heat."
"254","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray while wearing his shoes?"" He replied: ""Yes! (He used to pray with them on)."
"255","Hammam bin Harith says: I saw Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) urinating, then he performed ablution and wiped over his socks, then stood up to pray. After the prayer, people asked him about this matter, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) doing the same. People liked this hadith because Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) was the last to embrace Islam."
"256","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhaina (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer, he would keep a gap between his arms so much so that the whiteness of his armpits became visible."
"257","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays our (kind of) prayer, faces our Qiblah, and eats our slaughtered animals, then he is a Muslim, for whom is the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So do not betray Allah regarding His protection."
"258","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he was asked about a man who had performed Tawaf of the Ka'bah for Umrah but had not performed Tawaf (Sa'i) between Safa and Marwah, whether he could approach his wife (or not?). He replied that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came (from Madinah), performed Tawaf of the Ka'bah seven times (i.e., circumambulated the Ka'bah seven times), offered two rak'ahs of prayer behind Maqam Ibrahim, and performed Tawaf (Sa'i) between Safa and Marwah. And indeed, in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there is an excellent example for you."
"259","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says` When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, he supplicated in all its corners and did not pray until he came out of the Ka'bah. Then, when he came out, he prayed two rak'ahs facing the Ka'bah and said that this is the Qiblah."
"260","Narrated by Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen or seventeen months. (Until Allah revealed verses 142 to 144 of Surah Al-Baqarah.) This hadith has already been mentioned before (see the Book: Explanation of Faith... Chapter: Establishing Prayer is part of Faith...). And the wording in both narrations is different."
"261","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer voluntary prayers on his mount, facing in whichever direction it turned. But when he intended to offer an obligatory prayer, he would dismount and face the Qiblah."
"262","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered prayer. Ibrahim is the narrator from Alqamah, and Alqamah is the narrator from Sayyiduna Ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them), who says: I do not know whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) increased or decreased (something) in the prayer. Then, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished the prayer with salam, it was said to him, “O Messenger of Allah! Has something new happened in the prayer?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “What is that?” The people said, “You offered such and such amount of prayer.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew his feet together, faced the qiblah, and performed two prostrations, then gave salam. Then, when he turned towards us, he said, “If any new command had been given regarding the prayer, I would have informed you (beforehand), but I am only a human being like you; just as you forget, I also forget. Therefore, when I forget, remind me, and when any one of you is uncertain in his prayer, he should try to determine what is correct and complete his prayer accordingly, then give salam and perform two prostrations (of forgetfulness).”"
"263","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I agreed with my Lord in three matters. (Once) I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! If only we could take the Maqam Ibrahim as a place of prayer."" Then this verse was revealed: ""And take the Maqam Ibrahim as a place of prayer."" (Al-Baqarah: 125) And the verse of hijab was also revealed according to my wish. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! If only you would command your wives to observe veiling, because both righteous and wicked people speak to them."" So the verse of hijab was revealed. And (once) the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gathered together out of excitement before him, so I said to them, ""If he (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) divorces you, soon his Lord will give him better wives than you in your place."" (At-Tahrim: 5) So this very verse was revealed."
"264","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw some spittle in the direction of the Qiblah, and it was displeasing to him. So much so that (the effect of anger) appeared on his blessed face. Then he (peace be upon him) stood up and cleaned it with his own hand. Then he said: ""When any of you stands in his prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, or (he peace be upon him said) his Lord is between him and the Qiblah, so he should not spit in the direction of the Qiblah, but rather to his left side or under his foot."" Then he (peace be upon him) took the edge of his sheet, spat in it, and rubbed it, and said: ""Do like this."
"265","This same hadith about spitting is also narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him), but with these additional words: ""(During prayer) do not spit to your right side."
"266","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and burying it is its expiation."
"267","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You think I cannot see you from the front, but by Allah, neither your humility nor your bowing is hidden from me, and indeed I see you from behind my back (as well)."
"268","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that (on one occasion) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) held a horse race between trained horses from (the place of) Hafya, and its end was at Thaniyyat al-Wada'. And for those horses that were not trained, he held a race from Thaniyya to the mosque of Banu Zuraiq. And Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was among those who participated in that horse race."
"269","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Bahrain. He (peace be upon him) said: ""Spread it out in the mosque."" And that (wealth) was more than any wealth that had ever been brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) up to that time. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came for prayer and did not even look towards it. Then when he (peace be upon him) had finished the prayer, he came and sat by it, and whoever he saw, he would certainly give to him. Meanwhile, Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Give me (also), for I have paid my own ransom and the ransom of Aqil."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take it."" He took with both hands into his garment, then tried to lift it but could not. Then he said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Order someone among them to help me lift it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""No."" He said, ""Then you yourself place it on me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""No."" So Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) dropped some of it and tried to lift it (and still could not), so he said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Order someone among them to help me lift it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again said, ""No."" He said, ""Then you yourself lift it and place it on me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused. Then Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) dropped some more from it. After that, he lifted it and placed it on his shoulder and went away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), amazed at his greed, kept looking at him from behind until he disappeared from us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave from there until not a single dirham remained."
"270","Sayyiduna Mahmood bin Rabee’ Al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna ‘Itbaan bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who was among the Ansari companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who participated in Badr, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I find my eyesight to be weak and I also lead my people in prayer. So, when it rains, the valley that lies between me and them flows, and I cannot go to their mosque to lead them in prayer. So, O Messenger of Allah! I wish that you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to me and pray in my house so that I may take that place as a prayer area.” Sayyiduna ‘Itbaan (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, “I will do so, insha’Allah, soon.” So he says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came when the sun had risen. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission to enter, so I gave him permission. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house and had not yet sat down when he said, “In which part of your house do you wish me to pray?” So Sayyiduna ‘Itbaan (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I pointed to a place in the house, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood there and said Allahu Akbar. We formed a row behind him. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak’ahs and then gave salam. Sayyiduna ‘Itbaan (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we detained him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for khazeerah (a dish made of meat and flour) which we had prepared for him. Then he says that several people from the neighborhood gathered in the house, and one of them said, “Where is Malik bin Dukhshum?” or (he said), “Where is Ibn Dukhshum?” So another among them said, “He is a hypocrite; he does not love Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Do not say this. Have you not seen that he said La ilaha illallah seeking Allah’s pleasure?” That person said, “Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) know best, but outwardly we have seen his inclination and goodwill towards the hypocrites.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has made the Fire forbidden for the person who says La ilaha illallah, seeking thereby Allah’s pleasure.”"
"271","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): Umm Habiba and Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with them) saw a church in Abyssinia in which there were pictures. They mentioned this to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and he said: ""When a righteous man among those people died, they would build a mosque over his grave and make these pictures in it. These people are the worst of creatures in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"272","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah (after migrating), he stayed in the upper part of Madinah among a tribe called Banu Amr bin Awf, and he stayed among those people for fourteen nights. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Banu Najjar, so they came with their swords hanging. Now, it is as if I am looking at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he is on his mount and Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) is riding behind him, and the group of Banu Najjar is around the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted at the house of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) and unloaded his belongings. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked that wherever the time for prayer came, he would pray there, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would also pray in the places where goats were kept. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the construction of a mosque. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for the people of Banu Najjar and said: ""O Banu Najjar! Sell me this garden of yours."" They replied, ""By Allah! We will not take its price except from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."" Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: In that (garden) were things I am telling you about, that is, graves of polytheists, ruins, and date-palm trees. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the graves of the polytheists be dug up. Then he ordered that the ruins be leveled and the trees be cut down, and the date-palm trees were set up in the direction of the qiblah of the mosque, and its enclosure was made with stones. The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) began to bring stones, reciting rajaz verses, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with them and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: ""The real benefit is the benefit of the Hereafter. O Allah, grant forgiveness to the Ansar and the Muhajirin."
"273","(Narrator of the hadith, Nafi', says:) Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) prayed towards his camel (using it as a sutrah) and said that he had seen the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do so."
"274","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""While I was praying, Hell was presented before me."
"275","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Offer some of your prayers in your houses and do not make them graves."
"276","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was overtaken by (the illness of death), he began to place his cloak over his face. Then, when he felt heat from it, he would remove it from his face. Then, in this state, he said: ""May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians, for they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) was warning against their actions."
"277","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that there was an Abyssinian slave girl belonging to an Arab tribe. They had set her free, but she used to stay with them. She narrates that (once) a girl from that tribe went out, and she had a red leather amulet on her body. She says that she herself took it off, or it fell from her, then a kite passed by that way and the amulet was lying (on the ground). The kite thought it was meat and snatched it away. She says that those people searched for it but could not find it, so they accused me of taking it. She says that they started searching me, even to the extent that they looked at her private parts. She says, ""By Allah, I was standing with them when suddenly that kite passed by and dropped it (the amulet)."" She says that the amulet fell among them. She says, ""I said, 'This is the very thing for which you accused me. You suspected me, although I was innocent, and here it is.'"" Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that then she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and accepted Islam, so she had a tent in the mosque, or (she said) a small room. And she used to come to me and talk to me. And whenever she came to me, she would always say, ""The day of the amulet is one of the wonders of our Lord's ... powers ... Be aware, it is He who saved me from the city of disbelief ..."" Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says, ""I asked her, 'What is the matter that whenever you come to me, you always say this?' So she narrated this story to me."
"278","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) and did not find Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) at home, so he (peace be upon him) said: “Where is your cousin?” She replied that something (a dispute) had happened between me and him, so he became angry with me and left, and did not sleep here. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a person: “See where he is.” He (the person) went and came back and said that he is sleeping in the mosque. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went (to the mosque) and he (Ali) was lying down, his cloak had fallen off his side and there was dust on his (body), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to brush the dust off him and was saying: “O Abu Turab! Get up. O Abu Turab! Get up.”"
"279","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Al-Salmi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any of you enters the mosque, he should pray two rak'ahs before sitting down."
"280","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the mosque was built of unbaked bricks, its roof was made of palm branches, and its pillars were of palm wood. Then, Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) did not make any addition to it, and Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) made an addition to it and rebuilt it with unbaked bricks and palm branches, in accordance with the building during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and again set up wooden pillars. After that, Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) changed it and made many additions to it, and built its walls with decorated stones and plaster, and its roof with teakwood (a type of wood)."
"281","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) began to narrate a hadith (one day) until he reached the account of the construction of the mosque (the Prophet's Mosque). He said: We used to lift one brick each, and Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to lift two bricks. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw him, he began to dust the dirt off his (body) and kept saying: ""Woe to Ammar's distress! A rebellious group will kill him; they will call him towards Paradise, and he will call them towards Hellfire."" Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Ammar used to say: ""I seek refuge with Allah from tribulations."
"282","Narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) that when people were talking about him, at the time when he (Uthman) built the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""You have said much (about me), although I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Whoever builds a mosque, seeking the pleasure of Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise like it.'"
"283","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): A man was passing through the mosque and he had some arrows with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""Hold them by their tips (the part that can injure someone)."
"284","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever passes through any of our mosques or markets with an arrow should hold its tips, lest he injure a Muslim brother with his own hand."
"285","‘Sayyiduna Hassan bin Thabit Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) asked Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) for testimony, saying: “I ask you by Allah, (tell me) did you hear from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say to me: ‘O Hassan! Respond on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (to the polytheists), O Allah! Support Hassan with the Holy Spirit.’” So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Yes (I heard it).”"
"286","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) one day at the door of my room, and the Abyssinians were playing in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was shielding me with his cloak, and I was watching their play. In another narration, it is mentioned that they were playing with their swords."
"287","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he demanded repayment of a debt from Ibn Abi Hadrad in the mosque. Their voices became loud until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard them while he was in his house. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to them, lifted the curtain of his chamber, and called out: ""O Ka'b!"" He replied, ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Reduce some of your debt,"" and he gestured, meaning half (reduce it by half). Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have reduced it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) then said (to Ibn Abi Hadrad): ""Get up and pay it."
"288","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): A black man or a black woman used to sweep the mosque. When he (or she) died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about him (or her). The people said, ""He (or she) has died."" He said, ""Why did you not inform me? (Well then) show me his (or her) grave."" So the people showed it to him, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the funeral prayer for him (or her)."
"289","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the verses of Surah Al-Baqarah regarding usury were revealed, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) went towards the mosque and recited these verses before the people. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) prohibited the trade of alcohol."
"290","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A rebellious jinn came before me last night (or he said a similar word) to interrupt my prayer, but Allah gave me control over him. I intended to tie him to one of the pillars of the mosque so that you all could see him in the morning. Then I remembered the supplication of my brother Solomon (peace be upon him): 'My Lord, grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me.' (Surah Sad 35) (So the Prophet, peace be upon him, humiliated him and let him go.)"
"291","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that on the day of (the Battle of) Khandaq, Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) was wounded in the median vein (a name of a vein), so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) set up a tent in the mosque so that he could visit him closely. Then suddenly, while there was also a tent of Banu Ghifar in the mosque, blood started flowing towards them, so those people said, ""O people of the tent! What is this that is coming to us from your side?"" (When they looked,) they saw that blood was flowing from the wound of Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), and thus he was martyred from this wound."
"292","Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I was ill, so he said: ""Perform Tawaf riding behind the people."" So I performed Tawaf, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying in a corner of the Ka'bah. He was reciting Surah At-Tur."
"293","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that two persons from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left from the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark night. (One of them was Sayyiduna ‘Abbad bin Bishr, may Allah be pleased with him, and I think the other was Sayyiduna Usayd bin Hudayr, may Allah be pleased with him.) And with both of them were two lamps (of light) which were shining in front of them. Then when they separated, one (lamp) remained with each of them, until they reached their homes."
"294","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon one day and said: ""Indeed, Allah, the Exalted, gave a servant the choice between (the world) and that which is with Allah, so he chose that which is with Allah."" Upon hearing this, the leader of the believers, Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), began to weep. I said to myself, ""What is making this old man cry? If Allah gave a servant the choice between the world and that which is with Allah, and he chose that which is with Allah, then what is there to cry about?"" But in the end, it became clear that the servant referred to was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) himself, and Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) was the most knowledgeable among us. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Bakr! Do not weep. Indeed, the person who has done the greatest favor to me, with his companionship and his wealth, is Abu Bakr as-Siddiq. And if I were to take a close friend (khalil) from my ummah, I would certainly take Abu Bakr, but the brotherhood of Islam and its love is sufficient. And in the mosque, all the doors except the door of Abu Bakr should be closed."
"295","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), during his illness in which he passed away, came out with his head tied with a bandage and sat on the pulpit. Then he praised and glorified Allah, then said: ""O people! There is no one who has done more favor to me with his life and wealth than Abu Bakr, and if I were to take anyone from among the people as a close friend (khalil), I would certainly have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but the brotherhood of Islam is superior. Close every window in this mosque except the window of Abu Bakr."
"296","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, he called for Uthman bin Talha (may Allah be pleased with him). He opened the (Ka'bah's) door, then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Bilal, Usama bin Zaid, and Uthman bin Talha (may Allah be pleased with them all) went inside. After that, the door was closed. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed there for a little while, after which everyone came out. Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that I hurried towards the Ka'bah and asked Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), so he informed me that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed inside the Ka'bah. I asked, ""At which place?"" He said, ""Between the two pillars."" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says, ""I missed asking him how much prayer the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had performed."
"297","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): A man asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was on the pulpit about the prayer at night. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Pray two by two (rak'ahs)."" Then when any one of you fears that morning is approaching, let him pray one rak'ah, and that one rak'ah will make what he has prayed odd (witr) for him. And Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to say: ""Make your last prayer at night witr, because the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered this."
"298","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zaid Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, lying on his back in the mosque with one of his legs placed over the other."
"299","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer in congregation is superior in reward by twenty-five (25) degrees to the prayer offered at home or in the market, because when one of you performs ablution and does it well, and then goes to the mosque with the sole intention of offering prayer, then for every step he takes, Allah raises him one degree and forgives him one sin, until he enters the mosque. When he enters, he is considered to be in prayer as long as the prayer keeps him there, and the angels continue to pray for him as long as he remains at the place where he offered the prayer. The angels pray: ""O Allah! Forgive his sins. O Allah! Have mercy on him."" (This prayer continues) as long as he does not lose his ablution."
"300","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""A believer to another believer is like a building, each part of which strengthens the other."" And he (peace be upon him) interlaced his fingers."
"301","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two prayers after the sun had passed its zenith. He led us in two rak‘ahs and then said the salam. Then he stood by a piece of wood that was fixed in the mosque and leaned against it as if he was angry, and he placed his right hand on his left and interlaced his fingers (i.e., he inserted the fingers of one hand into those of the other), and he placed his right cheek on the back of his left palm. The hasty people left through the doors of the mosque. The companions said, “Has the prayer been shortened?” Among the people were Abu Bakr and ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), but they were afraid to speak to him. Among them was a man whose hands were long, and he was called Dhu’l-Yadayn. He said, “O Messenger of Allah! Did you forget, or has the prayer been shortened?” He said, “I did not forget, nor has the prayer been shortened (to my knowledge).” Then he (the Prophet) said (to the people), “Is it as Dhu’l-Yadayn says?” The people said, “Yes.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved forward and completed what he had left of the prayer. After that, he said the salam, then said the takbeer and performed a prostration like his usual prostrations or perhaps a little longer. Then he raised his head and said the takbeer, then said the takbeer again and performed another prostration like his usual prostrations or perhaps a little longer. Then he raised his head and said the takbeer, and then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the salam."
"302","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them)` used to pray at certain places on the road and would say that he had seen the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) praying at those places."
"303","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ‘Umrah or Hajj, he would also stop at (the place of) Dhul-Hulaifah. And when he returned from any expedition and passed through that route, or was on Hajj or ‘Umrah, he would descend into the valley. Then, when he ascended from the depth of the valley, he would make the camel kneel at that Batha’ which is on the edge of the valley towards the east. Then, in the last part of the night, he would rest there until morning came. (This place where the Prophet, peace be upon him, used to rest) is not near the mosque built of stones, nor on the mound on which the mosque is situated. Rather, there was a spring at that place, and Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray near it, and there were some sand dunes inside it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray there. Then, a flood came from the Batha’ and flowed until it reached the place where Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray."
"304","´Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them):` The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered prayer at the place where the small mosque is, which is near the mosque that is on the elevation of Rauha. And Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) knew the place where the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed. He used to say that it is on your right side when you stand to pray in the mosque, and this mosque is on the right edge of the road when you are going towards Makkah. There is a distance of about a stone's throw between it and the big mosque."
"305","`Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)` used to pray at the foot of that hill which is at the far end of Rauha, and (while going to Makkah) the edge of this hill is between the mosque and the far end of Rauha. And at that place, another mosque has been built, but Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not pray in that mosque; rather, he would leave it behind on his left side and would go ahead to pray specifically at the foot of the hill. And Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to set out from Rauha in the morning, and he would not pray the Zuhr prayer until he reached that place, so he would pray Zuhr there. And when coming from Makkah, if he reached that place a little before Fajr or in the last part of the night, he would stay there until he prayed the Fajr prayer at that place."
"306","Narrated Abdullah (bin Umar) (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (ﷺ) used to dismount near (the place of) Ruwaitha, on the right side of the road and in front of the road, under a dense tree, in a spacious and soft area, until he would come out from that mound which is about two miles from Buraid Ruwaitha. The upper part of that tree is broken, and it is bent in the middle, standing on its root, and there are many (sand) mounds at its root."
"307","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also offered prayer at the edge of that mound which is behind (the place) ‘Arj, when you are going towards (the village of) Hazbah. Near this mosque, there are two or three graves, and stones are placed on the graves. (There, the Prophet, peace be upon him, offered prayer on the right side of the road, near the stones of the road, between those very stones.) After the sun had passed its zenith at noon, Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) would depart from the place of ‘Arj and offer the Zuhr prayer in this mosque (meaning that a mosque had been built between those stones)."
"308","`Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped in that valley which is near Harshi (mountain), on the right side of the road, near the trees. The valley is adjacent to the edge of Harshi (mountain), and between it and the road there is a distance of about an arrow's shot. And Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to pray near that tree which was closest to the road among all the trees and was the tallest among them."
"309","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at this stream which is at the end of Maraz-Zahran towards Madinah, when a person descends from the mountains of Safradat. The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to stay on the left side of the road within the enclosure of this stream, when you are going towards Makkah. The place where the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stayed and the road are separated only by the distance of a stone's throw."
"310","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stay at (the place of) Dhi Tuwa and would spend the night there until morning came, and he would offer the morning prayer there (this was) when he came to Makkah. And the place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray is on a hard hill, not in the mosque that has been built there, but rather below it, on that same hard hill."
"311","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the two corners of this mountain, the corner which is between this mountain and the big mountain towards the Kaaba. Then he left the mosque that was built there to his left, the mosque that is towards the mound, and the place where the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed is below it, on top of the black mound, leaving about ten yards or so from the mound. Then, face towards those two corners of the mountain which are between you and the Kaaba and pray."
"312","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would go out (to lead the prayer) on the day of Eid, he would order that a harbah (small spear) be fixed in front of him, and he would pray facing towards it, and the people would be behind him. And he (peace and blessings be upon him) would do the same while traveling. From this, the leaders have adopted this practice (i.e., keeping a spear with them)."
"313","Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led the people in prayer at Batha. He performed two rak‘ahs of Zuhr and two rak‘ahs of ‘Asr, while a spear was fixed in front of him, and women and donkeys were passing in front of him."
"314","Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the space between the place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray and the wall was enough for a goat to pass through."
"315","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to relieve himself, I and a boy used to follow him, carrying a stick with a hook, or a staff, or a spear, and we had a water skin with us. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished relieving himself, we would hand him the water skin."
"316","Narrated from Sayyiduna Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to pray near the pillar which was close to the Mushaf (in Masjid Nabawi). So he was asked, “O Abu Muslim! (I, Yazid bin Abi Ubaidah,) see that you try to pray near this pillar?” He replied, “I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trying to pray near it.”"
"317","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)` narrates the hadith about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering the Ka'bah, that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah. I asked Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) (when he came out), ""What did the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do (inside the Ka'bah)?"" Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) said that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took one pillar to his left, one pillar to his right, and three pillars behind him, and he prayed, and at that time the Ka'bah was built on six pillars. In another narration (Imam Malik, may Allah have mercy on him, says), he took two pillars to his right."
"318","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) would make his mount sit crosswise and would pray facing it. (Ubaidullah, the narrator, asked Nafi', the narrator) that when the mounts would go away to graze (then what would the Prophet, peace be upon him, do?) He replied that the Prophet (peace be upon him) would take the saddle, then would pray towards its rear part or (he said) towards its last part, and Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would do the same."
"319","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Have you people considered us equal to dogs and donkeys? Indeed, I have seen myself lying on the bed and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come and stand in the middle of the bed (to pray), and I disliked being in front of him (during prayer), so I would slip away towards the legs of the bed until I would be outside my blanket."
"320","´Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him)` was praying on Friday facing something that concealed him from the people. Then a young man from (the tribe of) Banu Abi Mu‘ayt wanted to pass in front of him, so Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) pushed him in the chest. The young man did not find any way to pass except in front of him, so again he tried to pass, and Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) pushed him even harder than before. At this, the young man insulted Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him). After that, he went to Marwan and complained to him about what had happened with Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him), and after him, Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) also went to Marwan. So Marwan said, “O Abu Sa‘id! What is the matter between you and your brother’s son?” Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ‘When any one of you prays towards something that screens him from the people, and someone wants to pass in front of him, he should push him away, and if he refuses, then he should fight him, for he is only a devil.’”"
"321","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Juhaim (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If the one passing in front of a person who is praying knew how much sin he incurs, then surely it would be better for him to stand still for forty ... than to pass in front of him."" (Abu Nadr) the narrator of the hadith says: I do not know whether he said forty days, or forty months, or forty years."
"322","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would be performing prayer and I would be lying on my side on the bed in front of him. Then, when he intended to perform Witr, he would wake me up, so I would also perform Witr."
"323","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, and while in that state, he would carry Umamah bint Zaynab bint Rasulullah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the daughter of Abu al-As bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams. Then, when he would go into prostration, he would put her down, and when he stood up, he would pick her up. (Sayyidah Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her) was the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Umamah was his granddaughter, and Abu al-As was his son-in-law.)"
"324","The hadith of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, regarding the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) supplicating against the Quraysh, which he did on the day they placed the entrails upon him, has already been mentioned (see the Book: Description of Ablution... Chapter: If impurity or carrion is placed on the back of one who is praying, his prayer is not invalidated). And in this narration, it is further stated that after that, they were dragged and thrown into the well of Badr. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Curse be upon the people of this well."
